/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Every imaging system has inherent imperfections that cause blurring. The Point Spread Function \(PSF\) mathematically represents how a single point of light is spread in the final image. A narrow PSF corresponds to a sharper system, while a wider PSF indicates blur due to lens aberrations, motion, or diffraction. Understanding PSF is important in image restoration, deblurring, and super-resolution, as it provides a model of how images degrade during acquisition.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
